questions.answer:
(i) Propane: CH_{3}–CH_{2}–CH_{3}, C_{3}H_{8}
(ii) Propene: CH_{3}–CH=CH_{2}, C_{3}H_{6}
(iii) Propyne: CH_{3}–C≡CH, C_{3}H_{4}

1. A straight chain: CH_{3}–CH_{2}–CH_{2}–CH_{2}–CH_{3}
2. A branch on the second carbon: CH_{3}–CH(CH_{3})–CH_{2}–CH_{3}
3. Two branches on the middle carbon: C(CH_{3})_{4}, a central carbon joined to four CH_{3} groups.
All three have the formula C_{5}H_{12}.
